From jmacdon at med.umich.edu  Fri Dec 23 14:55:04 2005
From: jmacdon at med.umich.edu (James W. MacDonald)
Date: Fri, 23 Dec 2005 08:55:04 -0500
Subject: [BioC] justRMA and custom CDF
In-Reply-To: <6.2.3.4.0.20051223185123.01cd0a88@worra.ichr.uwa.edu.au>
References: <6.2.3.4.0.20051223185123.01cd0a88@worra.ichr.uwa.edu.au>
Message-ID: <43AC01B8.7020001@med.umich.edu>

Anthony Bosco wrote:
> Hi ,
> 
> I would like to analyse a large Affymetrix dataset with justRMA 
> function and a custom CDF.
> 
> Is this possible?

Yes it is possible, but you will have to convert the cdf into either a 
cdfenv or a cdf package first. See ?make.cdf.env and ?make.cdf.package 
in the matchprobes package.

One caveat; if you make the package you should not specify a name, as 
make.cdf.package will name it correctly for you. However, if you are 
making an environment, you need to specify a name which should be the 
name of the cdf file minus the .cdf portion. Note that the name is 
case-sensitive. If you mis-name the cdfenv, then the affy package will 
not be able to find it.

Best,

Jim


