There isn't necessarily a "procedure".  You could use the genbank accession
numbers from the three arrays as input to stanford Source to get a mapping
to recent unigene build.  You could also use the annotation packages from
Bioconductor to do the same thing, though I'm not sure what operon set you
are using and whether there is an annotation package available for it.  Once
you have each array mapped to a common identifier, you can use the functions
"match", "intersect", "union", and "%in%" to determine overlaps in the
different sets.

Sean


